<title>USA: BEFORE THE BELL - Santa Fe up on Homestake bid.</title>
<headline>BEFORE THE BELL - Santa Fe up on Homestake bid.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-12-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Santa Fe Pacific Gold Corp shares gained 1-1/2 to 16-3/4 preceding Monday's market open on news the company agreed to merge with Homestake Mining Corp in a stock swap worth about $2.3 billion.</p>
<p>The deal values Santa Fe at $17.42 per share, almost $2 per share more than Newmont Mining Corp's unsolicited stock bid for Santa Fe made last Thursday.</p>
<p>Santa Fe never formally responded to the Newmont offer.</p>
<p>Meanwhile, Homestake traded 1/2 lower at 15-1/8 and Newmont shares were idle.</p>
</text>
